  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "1e02e5f3e0ee"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "camel toolbox only ships with support for XSLT 1.0 which is ancient by modern standards. Requests have come in for more modern support for 2 and 3. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "The Solr indexer applies the transform via Camel's plain XSLT component — ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "SolrRouter.java:170",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " does ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "toD(\"xslt:${header.CamelIndexingTransformation}\")",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ", and the project depends on ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "camel-xslt",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " (",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://claude.ai/epitaxy/local_8d990485-d089-4753-b36e-65afd03eaadd"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "pom.xml:161",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ").",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "af19a41216bd"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "That component delegates to the JDK's built-in JAXP ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "TransformerFactory",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " (the Xalan-derived XSLTC processor bundled with the JVM), which implements only XSLT 1.0 / XPath 1.0. Saxon is nowhere on the classpath, so there's no XSLT 2.0/3.0 support.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "787c7a16ea80"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If you wanted 2.0/3.0 support, the standard route would be swapping in ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "camel-xslt-saxon",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " and using ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "xslt-saxon:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " URIs — Saxon-HE would give you XSLT 3.0. That's worth keeping in mind for the Camel 4 upgrade too, since the component split (",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "camel-xslt",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " vs ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "camel-xslt-saxon",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ") carries over there unchanged.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
